// EXPECT: [E015]
// The module boundary: a call to a function defined in ANOTHER module contributes only its declared
// contract. `k` returns 5, but it declares only i32, so `a / k()` may divide by zero as far as this
// module is concerned. Before the rule, the compiler read k's body across the boundary and accepted
// this, so an edit inside boundary_lib (returning 0) would have flipped this caller's verdict.
// The allowed side is declared_range_crosses_module_pass.ln.
import tests.modules.boundary_lib.{k}
func divide(a i32) i32 { return a / k() }
func main() i32 { return divide(10) - 2 }
